# Licence

Copyright (c) 2026 the author of clip dashboard. All rights reserved.

This is **not** open-source software. The source is provided to you because
the software cannot work without it: it runs on your own computer, against
your own platform credentials, and you have to be able to read and configure
what you are running. Being able to read it is the point. Being able to pass
it on is not.

## What one licence lets you do

A licence covers **one operator**: one person, publishing to accounts that
person owns or is authorised to act for.

You may:

- run it on any computer you control, as many as you like, for that one
  operator's accounts;
- read, audit and modify your copy, for your own use;
- keep running the version you were given, for as long as you like, including
  after the licence ends by expiry rather than by breach.

## What it does not let you do

You may not:

- give, sell, sub-licence, rent, publish or otherwise pass the software or any
  part of it to anyone else, modified or not;
- run it on behalf of other people as a service, agency offering, or managed
  posting arrangement for third-party accounts, unless your licence says in
  writing that it covers that;
- remove or defeat the credit line and source link the software writes beside
  every clip;
- present it as your own work, or re-licence it.

One licence is one operator. An agency posting for a roster of clients needs a
licence that says so.

## The footage is not yours and this licence does not make it yours

The software cuts short videos out of **other people's** public broadcasts. It
acquires no rights in that footage and can grant you none. Everything in the
"The operator is responsible for what they publish" section of `TERMS.md`
applies to you, and nothing in this licence narrows it. What you publish, and
any claim arising from it, is yours.

## No warranty

Provided **as is, without warranty of any kind**, express or implied,
including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and
non-infringement. The author is not liable for any claim, damages or other
liability arising from the software or its use.

It depends on third-party APIs — Twitch's, YouTube's, TikTok's, Meta's — that
can change, throttle or withdraw access at any time, and on each platform
granting you your own developer access. None of that is promised here, and no
refund is implied by any of it failing.

## If you breach this

The licence ends. You stop using the software and delete your copies. Nothing
you published before that point is clawed back.

